generics — Concept page for generic type parameters and bounds.

Syntax:
  interface Slot<T> {
    value: T
  }
  
  class Box<T extends Named> {
    value: T
  }
  
  implements<T extends Named> Printable for Box<T> {
    function display(self) -> string {
      return self.value.name
    }
  }

Generics are declared where the parameter is introduced: `class Box<T>`, `interface Slot<T>`, `function get<T>(value: T) -> T`, and top-level `implements<T extends Bound> Interface for Wrapper<T> { ... }`. In an `implements<T>` block, the binder goes immediately after `implements`, before the interface target; each bound parameter must be used in the `for` type so the implementation can be matched. Use `T extends Interface<Assoc = Type>` for bounds with associated type constraints.
